Package: spatialMIFtools
Title: Patient-Level Spatial Analysis of Multiplex Tissue Imaging Data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Sagnik", "Bhadury", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "sagnikbhadury@users.noreply.github.com")
Description: Patient-aware analysis of two-dimensional multiplex tissue imaging
    data. Functions construct area-normalized phenotype-density grids,
    within-image epithelial-density zones, recurrent spatial neighborhoods,
    ridge conditional networks, total-cellularity-adjusted networks,
    patient-level pathology contrasts, ordered zone interactions, random-label
    cross-pair enrichment, label-permutation tests, and fully nested
    leave-one-patient-out prediction. The package keeps patients as independent
    sampling units and treats images and spatial bins as nested observations.
